settings.liquid:
{%- comment -%}
  Scoped with section.id resolved by Liquid at render time, NOT with a hardcoded
  template id. The brightening-glow page carries a style block written the other
  way and it has been dead ever since its template id changed - zero matches, so
  its image sits centre-cropped instead of pinned. A class selector is no good
  either here: it would hit the page hero as well, and the two bands want
  different mobile scrims.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > picture > img,
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > img { object-position: right center; }
@media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > div { max-width: clamp(320px, 44vw, 640px); }
}
@media screen and (max-width: 699px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media::before {
    background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(10,14,22,0.88) 0%, rgba(10,14,22,0.70) 45%, rgba(10,14,22,0.60) 100%);
  }
}
</style>
